  "text": {
    "work": "work",
    "card": "Toggle A and B to compare the AND, OR, XOR and NAND indicators.",
    "logic": "logic trainer",
    "truth": "truth table display",
    "wrong_phase": "Choose the toggle offer matching the current input phase.",
    "free_hand": "Put down an object so a hand is free to use an input switch.",
    "howto_toggle": "The two fixed input labels are A on the left and B on the right. A lever points toward the fixed ON line when on, and toward OFF when off. A is bit1 and B bit2 of the one input phase:0 both off,1 A only,2 B only,3 both on. Use the toggle offer for the current phase; it flips only that input. The four fixed output labels read AND, OR, XOR, NAND from left to right. A bright green inlay means true and a dark face means false. In phases0,1,2,3 the indicator maps are AND0001, OR0111, XOR0110, NAND1110. This local indexed learning display prescribes switch poses and indicator visibility together. It models no circuit, voltage, current, room illumination, remote control, reaction network, timing, autonomous work or general computation, and makes no physical-switch-contact guarantee."
